 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Ice Formation — Innate Technique (1st level)</em></p><blockquote><p>Your technique is beautiful in its simplicity, and the ability to make and control ice.</p></blockquote><p>Beginning at 1st level, your innate technique has allowed you to mess with the temperature around you, creating extreme levels of cold. As an action for 1 cursed energy, you can force creatures in a 10ft cone to make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failure, they take 1d10 cold damage and are restrained as ice covers part of their bodies. On a success, they take half as much damage and are not restrained.<br />\n The creature can make a Strength saving throw at the beginning of its turns to break the ice and end the restrained condition.<br />\n All ice created by your technique will last until you end it as a free action, a creature breaks it, or you are poisoned, incapacitated, or unconscious.<br />\n At 3rd level, the damage of this feature increases to 2d10, to 3d10 at 6th, to 4d10 at 10th, to 5d10 at 14th, and to 6d10 cold damage at 20th level.</p>",
   "chat": ""
  },
